WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.379
Not every public detail creates the same risk.

00:00:03.379 --> 00:00:07.887
Evaluation begins with sensitivity: could the information expose identity, access, location,

00:00:07.887 --> 00:00:10.346
relationships, internal operations, or security controls?

00:00:10.346 --> 00:00:15.264
Then consider who can use it, how easily it can be combined,

00:00:15.264 --> 00:00:17.722
and what harm could reasonably follow.

00:00:17.722 --> 00:00:18.952
Context changes risk.

00:00:18.952 --> 00:00:22.231
A generic technology name may be low sensitivity,

00:00:22.231 --> 00:00:28.378
while the same detail combined with an exposed service and unpatched version may require action.

00:00:28.378 --> 00:00:33.296
A public office address differs from a private residence or precise routine.

00:00:33.296 --> 00:00:38.214
Aggregation risk occurs when individually ordinary details combine into a sensitive picture.

00:00:38.214 --> 00:00:40.263
Usernames, photos, calendars, vendor references,

00:00:40.263 --> 00:00:46.000
and technical records can reveal relationships or timing that no one source states directly.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.279
Analysis should minimize unnecessary aggregation, especially about individuals.

00:00:49.279 --> 00:00:50.918
Assess timeliness and accuracy.

00:00:50.918 --> 00:00:53.377
Old records, cached pages, reused addresses,

00:00:53.377 --> 00:00:56.246
and abandoned profiles can misrepresent current conditions.

00:00:56.246 --> 00:01:02.393
Validate important findings with authoritative or independent sources and record when each source was observed.

00:01:02.393 --> 00:01:04.442
Separate relevant findings from noise.

00:01:04.442 --> 00:01:08.541
A useful finding connects to a legitimate security, privacy, safety,

00:01:08.541 --> 00:01:12.639
or business objective and has enough evidence to support action.

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:16.737
Popularity, novelty, or personal curiosity are not measures of relevance.

00:01:16.737 --> 00:01:20.016
Prioritize by likelihood, potential impact, exposure, and confidence.

00:01:20.016 --> 00:01:22.475
Describe uncertainty and avoid alarmist conclusions.

00:01:22.475 --> 00:01:26.983
Remediation should be proportionate: correct a stale page, restrict a document,

00:01:26.983 --> 00:01:29.852
secure an account, assign an asset owner,

00:01:29.852 --> 00:01:33.540
or investigate an exposed service through authorized internal processes.
